            <ArticleTitle>A case of miliary tuberculosis presenting with bowel perforation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tuberculosis is a disease that should never be underestimated. It can affect anybody at any age. Doctors in the West do not have much experience of peritonitis secondary to tuberculosis. It is a condition that requires urgent and aggressive management as it can be fatal, even in the young and fit, as this case report illustrates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
